From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AX23_V2_OPENWRT <ax23-v2-openwrt@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:08:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: ipq50xx: archer-ax23-v2: fix Wi-Fi LED phy
 mapping

The 5 GHz LED was bound to phy0tpt and the 2.4 GHz LED to phy1tpt, while
the comment argued that the 2.4 GHz radio registers first. All posted
boot logs show c000000.wifi (IPQ5018, 2.4 GHz) ahead of b00a040.wifi
(QCN6122, 5 GHz), so swap them. Still to be confirmed with both radios
up. Also update the header: the RTL8367S-VB probe has been observed on
hardware (AX21 v5 running AX23 v2 firmware), no EU unit report exists.
---
 .../qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-archer-ax23-v2.dts | 31 ++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-archer-ax23-v2.dts b/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-archer-ax23-v2.dts
index a70f45d68c..b8d916fffe 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-archer-ax23-v2.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-archer-ax23-v2.dts
@@ -5,12 +5,14 @@
  * SoC:    Qualcomm IPQ5018 (IPQ0509), Cortex-A53 dual-core
  * RAM:    256 MB DDR3 (CDT: AP-MP02.1_128M16_DDR3_LM256)
  * Flash:  SPI-NAND 128 MB, dual-image (rootfs + rootfs_1)
- * Switch: Realtek RTL8367 family D (chip ID 0x6642 per qca-ssdk.ko
- *         analysis; NOT yet read from the physical unit)
+ * Switch: Realtek RTL8367S-VB, family D (chip ID 0x6642). Probed as
+ *         "RTL8367S-VB" by rtl8365mb on an AX21 v5 that runs AX23 v2
+ *         firmware (third-party UART logs, forum t/254876).
  *         Trunk on GMAC1 -> UNIPHY0 -> CPU port 6, reset GPIO39.
  *         Trunk mode is HSGMII 2.5G -- see the note above &gmac1.
- *         Matches the stock running.dts forced-speed and physical
- *         clock measurement. UNVERIFIED on hardware (no UART yet).
+ *         GPIO33 cannot be an active-low switch reset on that unit: it
+ *         is driven low as the (off) 2.4 GHz LED while the switch works.
+ *         No test on an EU AX23 v2 unit has been reported.
  * WiFi:   IPQ5018 internal (ath11k) 2.4 GHz
  *         QCN6102 (qcn6122 fw) 5 GHz via PCIe
  * UART:   GPIO28 (RX) / GPIO29 (TX), 115200 8N1, 1.8V
@@ -133,24 +135,25 @@
 			gpios = <&tlmm 32 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * phyN numbering follows ieee80211_register_hw() order. In
+		 * every AX23 v2 boot log posted so far (forum t/254876) the
+		 * IPQ5018 2.4 GHz radio (c000000.wifi) finishes QMI ~0.5 s
+		 * before the QCN6122 (b00a040.wifi), so phy0 = 2.4 GHz and
+		 * phy1 = 5 GHz. The previous mapping (5 GHz on phy0) contradicted
+		 * its own comment. Not yet observed with both radios up:
+		 * confirm with `iw phy` on first boot with board data.
+		 */
 		led-wifi-5g {
 			label = "white:wlan5g";
 			gpios = <&tlmm 11 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
-			linux,default-trigger = "phy0tpt";
+			linux,default-trigger = "phy1tpt";
 		};
 
-		/*
-		 * phy1tpt is inferred, not boot-tested: &wifi (2.4GHz)
-		 * is registered before &wifi1 (5GHz) in this DTS, and
-		 * the 5GHz LED above already uses phy0tpt, so phy1 is
-		 * assumed to map to the 2.4GHz radio by registration
-		 * order. Confirm against actual phy0/phy1 enumeration
-		 * on first real boot with both radios up.
-		 */
 		led-wifi-2g {
 			label = "white:wlan2g";
 			gpios = <&tlmm 33 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
-			linux,default-trigger = "phy1tpt";
+			linux,default-trigger = "phy0tpt";
 		};
 	};
 };
